01:30:23,960 --> 01:30:24,280
Hello?

1376
01:30:26,740 --> 01:30:27,700
Oh, never mind.

1377
01:30:28,700 --> 01:30:29,480
I am good.

1378
01:30:30,540 --> 01:30:32,140
Let's take this shovel for a trip.

1379
01:30:34,040 --> 01:30:36,320
We're gonna need to make a stone here as well.

1380
01:30:40,620 --> 01:30:41,680
In fact, let's do that now.

1381
01:30:42,680 --> 01:30:43,880
Why are we delaying?

1382
01:30:52,710 --> 01:30:54,750
Probably... Why did I deposit the damn stone?

1383
01:30:55,170 --> 01:30:55,570
Shit.

1384
01:30:58,110 --> 01:30:58,950
Eat the chops.

1385
01:30:59,490 --> 01:31:01,490
Ah, but wait, save those chops for combat.

1386
01:31:02,250 --> 01:31:06,670
When we're just at home, hanging out, we don't really need to eat the good food.

1387
01:31:06,830 --> 01:31:07,590
We eat the bad food.

1388
01:31:09,090 --> 01:31:10,650
I need normal-ass stone.

1389
01:31:22,790 --> 01:31:24,250
And then we need this guy.

1390
01:31:40,810 --> 01:31:41,810
Much better, huh?

1391
01:31:43,050 --> 01:31:47,450
Although, running... Okay, that works really well.

1392
01:31:48,190 --> 01:31:50,730
Oh, just being able to sprint through the village is actually massive.

1393
01:31:51,770 --> 01:31:53,050
What a great change.

1394
01:31:55,650 --> 01:31:56,490
Good stuff.

1395
01:32:04,390 --> 01:32:06,810
Oh no, I can't... Oh, that's a disaster.

1396
01:32:07,590 --> 01:32:08,930
It's gonna look so bad.

1397
01:32:12,140 --> 01:32:12,800
Uh-oh.

1398
01:32:14,180 --> 01:32:14,660
No!

1399
01:32:15,480 --> 01:32:15,960
ODB!

1400
01:32:16,580 --> 01:32:17,520
Stay at home.

1401
01:32:18,080 --> 01:32:23,280
Do not be tempted by the wide, wide world.

1402
01:32:25,780 --> 01:32:28,380
I know it's exciting, but you gotta stay at home, okay?

1403
01:32:29,360 --> 01:32:31,240
You're not ready for that sort of thing yet.

1404
01:32:32,440 --> 01:32:33,960
Maybe one day when you grow up.

1405
01:32:35,420 --> 01:32:36,700
Maybe then I'll let you out.

1406
01:32:36,900 --> 01:32:39,980
And you can roam the land as a free animal.

1407
01:32:42,060 --> 01:32:43,220
What the hell are you doing here?

1408
01:32:45,840 --> 01:32:47,180
I didn't actually mean to do that.

1409
01:32:47,280 --> 01:32:48,180
It was a gut reaction.

1410
01:32:49,600 --> 01:32:51,280
I just needed to kill something, I guess.

1411
01:32:51,500 --> 01:32:53,840
It was a, you know... It happened.

1412
01:32:54,100 --> 01:32:54,740
What can I say?

1413
01:32:55,680 --> 01:32:57,020
So, clearing a path.

1414
01:32:57,200 --> 01:32:58,120
This is gonna be gone.

1415
01:32:58,940 --> 01:33:00,480
Get rid of all the shrubbery.

1416
01:33:02,860 --> 01:33:04,300
We hate shrubberies.

1417
01:33:08,180 --> 01:33:09,080
It's disappearing, good.

1418
01:33:09,740 --> 01:33:10,980
Now the path is gonna go like this.

1419
01:33:11,360 --> 01:33:12,440
Pretty much straight down.

1420
01:33:13,400 --> 01:33:15,600
Not entirely straight, that's gonna feel too artificial.

1421
01:33:15,800 --> 01:33:17,100
We need to bend it a little bit.

1422
01:33:18,140 --> 01:33:20,100
But other than that, pretty much straight.

1423
01:33:22,740 --> 01:33:23,780
Get rid of this one.

1424
01:33:25,260 --> 01:33:26,420
We get rid of Antoine.

1425
01:33:29,500 --> 01:33:29,900
Okay.

1426
01:33:32,660 --> 01:33:33,440
There we are.

1427
01:33:42,300 --> 01:33:42,660
Good.

1428
01:33:42,780 --> 01:33:43,260
Good enough.

1429
01:33:46,980 --> 01:33:50,340
By the way, I'm instinctively using the shovel to remove leaves.

1430
01:33:51,940 --> 01:33:53,800
Which, when you think about it, doesn't make much sense.

1431
01:33:53,920 --> 01:33:57,320
If you use a shovel in real life to remove leaves, it's kind of dumb.

1432
01:33:58,060 --> 01:33:59,700
I definitely need shears for this.

1433
01:34:02,920 --> 01:34:04,800
That is the correct gardening tool.

1434
01:34:07,680 --> 01:34:08,840
I just don't have them on me.

1435
01:34:12,320 --> 01:34:16,160
Okay, so the path is gonna go like... Where's my glass?

1436
01:34:17,080 --> 01:34:19,420
Oh my god, did I lose that as well?

1437
01:34:21,020 --> 01:34:21,560
Actually?

1438
01:34:24,200 --> 01:34:24,740
Everything.

1439
01:34:25,040 --> 01:34:26,160
I lost everything.

1440
01:34:31,460 --> 01:34:32,820
I'm not liking this.

1441
01:34:33,280 --> 01:34:35,040
Right here, this is making me unhappy.

1442
01:34:38,030 --> 01:34:39,590
That's making me angry.

1443
01:34:41,950 --> 01:34:42,690
Oh no.

1444
01:34:43,730 --> 01:34:46,310
Some kind of unknown emotion just swelled up inside of me.

1445
01:34:47,090 --> 01:34:47,830
That's better.

1446
01:34:49,490 --> 01:34:50,030
Okay.

1447
01:34:51,050 --> 01:34:53,050
Seeds, that is farming for sure.

1448
01:34:53,650 --> 01:34:54,830
Saplings belong up here.

1449
01:34:55,930 --> 01:34:56,730
Leads go there.

1450
01:35:01,220 --> 01:35:02,540
And do I have anything else?

1451
01:35:02,700 --> 01:35:03,100
Bones!

1452
01:35:03,380 --> 01:35:06,160
Ah, I wanted to keep those on me in case I find a doggo.

1453
01:35:07,680 --> 01:35:08,300
Ominous banner.

1454
01:35:08,980 --> 01:35:10,660
That should definitely go in construction.

1455
01:35:12,740 --> 01:35:13,400
Uh, no?

1456
01:35:13,660 --> 01:35:13,760
Where?

1457
01:35:15,040 --> 01:35:15,440
There.

1458
01:35:16,300 --> 01:35:17,500
Got seven of them now.

1459
01:35:18,600 --> 01:35:20,660
Maybe we should start hanging it all over the town.

1460
01:35:23,020 --> 01:35:27,500
Let these raiders know that, hey, we're your people, you know?

1461
01:35:29,450 --> 01:35:30,510
Maybe they won't attack them.

1462
01:35:32,310 --> 01:35:32,810
Ah, wait.

1463
01:35:32,890 --> 01:35:33,670
I needed to get shears.

1464
01:35:36,810 --> 01:35:37,730
Get the shears!

1465
01:35:38,290 --> 01:35:39,730
And there was something else I came back for.

1466
01:35:39,810 --> 01:35:40,230
What was it?

1467
01:35:41,850 --> 01:35:42,770
I was down here.

1468
01:35:44,790 --> 01:35:46,010
And I needed to do something.

1469
01:35:46,310 --> 01:35:47,290
I think it was shears.

1470
01:35:50,730 --> 01:35:58,070
Shears, shears, shears... At the seashore... None here, but look at this!

1471
01:35:58,670 --> 01:35:59,990
I remember how to make him.

1472
01:36:01,330 --> 01:36:02,770
Ah, we're gonna have to cannibalize!

1473
01:36:03,010 --> 01:36:03,690
Just a bit.

1474
01:36:04,250 --> 01:36:06,650
We're slowly chipping every block off of this thing.

1475
01:36:08,910 --> 01:36:09,690
I need it.

1476
01:36:14,050 --> 01:36:15,370
Okay, so we know how to make a bucket.

1477
01:36:15,530 --> 01:36:16,590
It's actually almost the same.

1478
01:36:18,030 --> 01:36:22,230
It's like, uh... There we go.

1479
01:36:24,050 --> 01:36:25,130
Sweet cakes.

1480
01:36:26,690 --> 01:36:27,710
Time to shear!

1481
01:36:33,210 --> 01:36:34,070
Let's do it.

1482
01:36:36,470 --> 01:36:38,310
Oh, that's so much better.

1483
01:36:38,870 --> 01:36:39,750
Holy crap.

1484
01:36:40,190 --> 01:36:42,370
This may be the first time I've ever sheared a tree.

1485
01:36:44,670 --> 01:36:45,990
That is wonderful.

1486
01:36:48,210 --> 01:36:52,070
Oh, it's like a... So much better.

1487
01:36:53,010 --> 01:36:54,270
My life has changed.

1488
01:36:55,670 --> 01:36:56,970
After all these years.

1489
01:36:58,570 --> 01:36:59,770
We're shearing the tree.

1490
01:37:02,140 --> 01:37:03,620
Imagine all the time I wasted.

1491
01:37:04,340 --> 01:37:07,000
Every time I had to approach a tree just to cut it down.

1492
01:37:08,000 --> 01:37:08,780
No more.

1493
01:37:09,240 --> 01:37:10,020
I'm free.

1494
01:37:11,040 --> 01:37:13,220
Not like ODB, but like ODD.

1495
01:37:13,820 --> 01:37:15,560
Because now I have the fucking shears.

1496
01:37:16,140 --> 01:37:17,500
And I know how to use them.

1497
01:37:18,040 --> 01:37:19,280
Also, I'm straying from the path.

1498
01:37:19,300 --> 01:37:20,220
I need to stay true.

1499
01:37:21,760 --> 01:37:26,380
We want to do an... I guess an SLJ, but not quite.

1500
01:37:27,040 --> 01:37:28,960
It needs to be a semi-SLJ.

1501
01:37:29,930 --> 01:37:30,410
SSLJ.

1502
01:37:31,010 --> 01:37:34,590
A very rare SLJ, but sometimes they need to be employed, you know?

1503
01:37:35,210 --> 01:37:40,030
You can't go around just utilizing a single Johnson variant.

1504
01:37:42,790 --> 01:37:44,210
Look how fast this goes.

1505
01:37:45,910 --> 01:37:47,050
You can do it while jumping.

1506
01:37:53,270 --> 01:37:54,350
Probably not worth it.

1507
01:37:56,930 --> 01:37:57,990
But it's fine.

1508
01:37:59,270 --> 01:37:59,890
Okay.

1509
01:38:00,570 --> 01:38:01,990
Path is being cleared.

1510
01:38:03,470 --> 01:38:05,230
Immediately cut through that bullshit.

1511
01:38:08,530 --> 01:38:10,230
Now when it's like this, I'll just leave it be.

1512
01:38:10,450 --> 01:38:11,370
It'll take care of itself.

1513
01:38:11,530 --> 01:38:14,850
It's just when it's, like, really annoying and I need to get rid of it quick.

1514
01:38:16,270 --> 01:38:18,630
Now, the shears are losing durability here.

1515
01:38:20,190 --> 01:38:21,770
I wonder if I can put mending on that.

1516
01:38:22,250 --> 01:38:24,770
Then again, why would I?

1517
01:38:24,890 --> 01:38:27,850
I never really shear anything that gives experience when I shear it.

1518
01:38:28,970 --> 01:38:34,170
Then again, you don't really need to kill things with the shear.

1519
01:38:35,010 --> 01:38:36,090
You just need to have it, right?

1520
01:38:36,270 --> 01:38:38,030
And as long as you gain experience, then it heals.

1521
01:38:39,710 --> 01:38:40,870
I think that's how that works.

1522
01:38:46,290 --> 01:38:47,150
This guy...

1523
01:38:53,260 --> 01:38:54,040
Look at that.

1524
01:38:54,140 --> 01:38:55,580
Did you see how fast I made my approach?

1525
01:38:56,120 --> 01:38:57,100
Into the trunk.

1526
01:38:58,800 --> 01:38:59,800
That is the way.

1527
01:39:00,980 --> 01:39:02,280
We're gonna fix this!

1528
01:39:03,820 --> 01:39:05,160
Remember all the troubles.

1529
01:39:05,980 --> 01:39:07,440
No fucking more.

1530
01:39:08,320 --> 01:39:09,240
No more.

1531
01:39:09,720 --> 01:39:11,380
We're fixing all the holes today.

1532
01:39:11,720 --> 01:39:12,580
Everything gets plugged.

1533
01:39:14,540 --> 01:39:15,620
Who would have thunk?

1534
01:39:16,340 --> 01:39:19,760
The solution had been to pluck the damn hole since day one.

1535
01:39:24,350 --> 01:39:26,270
The cause of all of my issues right here.

1536
01:39:29,610 --> 01:39:30,350
No more.

1537
01:39:33,850 --> 01:39:37,170
I can't tell you the catharsis I'm experiencing right now.

1538
01:39:37,330 --> 01:39:37,650
Oh god.

1539
01:39:38,450 --> 01:39:39,090
Can I shear you?

1540
01:39:44,410 --> 01:39:46,450
Kind of want to try shearing everything now.

1541
01:39:46,570 --> 01:39:47,110
Can I shear this?

1542
01:39:48,870 --> 01:39:49,750
Will it shear?

1543
01:39:53,370 --> 01:39:54,710
Okay, it's actually getting a little dark.

1544
01:39:55,730 --> 01:39:56,530
Time to head home.

1545
01:39:56,730 --> 01:39:58,110
I will close this one up as well.

1546
01:39:58,910 --> 01:40:03,170
This is just another potential enemy spawn, isn't it?

1547
01:40:04,510 --> 01:40:05,590
Enemy spawn down here.

1548
01:40:06,130 --> 01:40:06,990
Because of the darkness.

1549
01:40:08,550 --> 01:40:10,210
Especially... Actually, hold on, hold on, hold on, hold on.

1550
01:40:10,710 --> 01:40:13,430
When I close it up, I actually create darkness during the day.

1551
01:40:14,490 --> 01:40:15,470
Down there, right?

1552
01:40:15,630 --> 01:40:16,530
Because I'm closing it up.

1553
01:40:17,470 --> 01:40:20,470
We're going to need to either fill it up completely or put torches in there.

1554
01:40:22,520 --> 01:40:22,920
Whoops.

1555
01:40:30,800 --> 01:40:33,080
Oh, but then I pick up a bunch of spruce leaves.

1556
01:40:36,080 --> 01:40:36,820
Wait a second.

1557
01:40:37,740 --> 01:40:39,960
I have never had these in my inventory like this.

1558
01:40:41,520 --> 01:40:44,360
Usually when I destroy leaves, they just go gone, right?

1559
01:40:45,040 --> 01:40:46,840
That is a new discovery.

1560
01:40:47,200 --> 01:40:48,520
Did I actually unlock something with that?

1561
01:40:51,750 --> 01:40:52,150
Hmm.

1562
01:40:52,530 --> 01:40:54,590
I feel like I would have seen it pop up in the top, right?

1563
01:40:55,950 --> 01:40:56,790
And I didn't.

1564
01:40:57,290 --> 01:40:58,210
Why did I come back?

1565
01:41:00,910 --> 01:41:01,650
Oh, sleep.

1566
01:41:01,890 --> 01:41:02,050
Right.

1567
01:41:02,990 --> 01:41:04,490
Go to sleep and grab torches.

1568
01:41:04,910 --> 01:41:05,850
That's why I came back.

1569
01:41:06,970 --> 01:41:07,570
We're gonna sleep.

1570
01:41:07,770 --> 01:41:08,510
We're gonna torch.

1571
01:41:08,630 --> 01:41:10,090
I'm sleeping with the dirt in my hand.

1572
01:41:10,870 --> 01:41:12,250
That's just... weird.

1573
01:41:16,770 --> 01:41:18,290
Okay, is everything still okay?

1574
01:41:18,650 --> 01:41:18,890
ODB?

1575
01:41:19,630 --> 01:41:19,910
Ginny?

1576
01:41:21,750 --> 01:41:22,550
ODB is here somewhere.

1577
01:41:22,670 --> 01:41:24,290
You can see a little block.

1578
01:41:24,390 --> 01:41:25,270
Oh, right, right, right, right, right.

1579
01:41:25,650 --> 01:41:25,930
Spyglass.

1580
01:41:26,530 --> 01:41:27,450
That's what I wanted to do.

1581
01:41:29,090 --> 01:41:29,370
Spyglass.

1582
01:41:29,490 --> 01:41:30,290
Tell me I made one extra.

1583
01:41:32,980 --> 01:41:35,120
Why didn't past me think about this?

1584
01:41:35,800 --> 01:41:39,620
Okay, Spyglass needs... I'll do it purely from memory now.

1585
01:41:40,520 --> 01:41:41,180
This.

1586
01:41:42,480 --> 01:41:44,680
And it needs this.

1587
01:41:46,260 --> 01:41:50,840
And... I think... Iron?

1588
01:41:52,900 --> 01:41:53,780
Damn it.

1589
01:41:54,680 --> 01:41:56,140
Ah, two copper ingots!

1590
01:41:56,380 --> 01:41:57,000
Fuck you.

1591
01:41:57,240 --> 01:41:58,200
I had it.

1592
01:42:00,580 --> 01:42:01,300
Uh...

1593
01:42:04,530 --> 01:42:05,850
Okay, nice.

1594
01:42:06,150 --> 01:42:07,450
Oh, I feel whole again.

1595
01:42:09,130 --> 01:42:11,570
I actually do feel naked without the spyglass.

1596
01:42:15,270 --> 01:42:16,770
Look at this path being cleared.

1597
01:42:18,750 --> 01:42:21,570
Actually, this is going to look sick when you approach.

1598
01:42:21,890 --> 01:42:23,570
Dude, we're going to have a dock down here.

1599
01:42:24,470 --> 01:42:27,170
Oh man, this village is going to be banging.

1600
01:42:28,670 --> 01:42:31,710
And people in this village are gonna be banging.

1601
01:42:35,530 --> 01:42:38,010
And you know what we're gonna do on the stove with a pan?

1602
01:42:38,510 --> 01:42:41,690
We're gonna make mash and bangers.

1603
01:42:45,850 --> 01:42:51,130
This guy needs to go... Look, look, see how it touches these?

1604
01:42:51,290 --> 01:42:51,670
It's bad.

1605
01:42:52,470 --> 01:42:53,930
That means they'll never disappear.

1606
01:42:55,830 --> 01:42:56,550
Give me that.

1607
01:43:02,340 --> 01:43:05,860
In fact, what I'm doing right now is I'm essentially running out the red carpet, you know?

1608
01:43:18,980 --> 01:43:19,380
Okay.

1609
01:43:22,460 --> 01:43:23,480
Where's the fence?

1610
01:43:24,400 --> 01:43:24,800
Oh!

1611
01:43:25,020 --> 01:43:26,040
I left the fence open!

1612
01:43:26,820 --> 01:43:27,460
Oh no!

1613
01:43:30,400 --> 01:43:31,200
Uh-oh.

1614
01:43:31,500 --> 01:43:32,640
Hopefully nothing escaped.

1615
01:43:37,400 --> 01:43:39,380
See, this is why you get a spyglass.

1616
01:43:40,780 --> 01:43:41,820
Spyglass, huh?

1617
01:43:42,580 --> 01:43:43,720
That's why you get it.

1618
01:43:45,460 --> 01:43:46,380
Man, oh man.

1619
01:43:47,200 --> 01:43:48,460
That could have been a disaster.

1620
01:43:49,640 --> 01:43:51,280
Imagine if I left home right now.

1621
01:43:55,130 --> 01:43:56,390
Glad I just saw that.

1622
01:43:56,930 --> 01:43:57,410
Okay.

1623
01:43:58,210 --> 01:44:02,150
All the trees must go... Like a machine gun.

1624
01:44:14,710 --> 01:44:15,090
Nice.

1625
01:44:15,090 --> 01:44:18,250
And... this is sort of connected here, so this needs to go.

1626
01:44:20,650 --> 01:44:23,990
And the best part about this is that I'm getting a bunch of wood out of it, too.

1627
01:44:24,210 --> 01:44:25,330
That I need to build with.

1628
01:44:26,130 --> 01:44:28,010
It's actually such a win-win situation, this.

1629
01:44:28,870 --> 01:44:30,430
Feeding two birds with one scone.

1630
01:44:32,110 --> 01:44:34,310
Actually, we're probably feeding multiple birds.

1631
01:44:34,830 --> 01:44:35,570
More than two.

1632
01:44:52,040 --> 01:44:52,820
Go here.

1633
01:44:55,960 --> 01:44:56,620
Oh, yeah.

1634
01:44:58,220 --> 01:44:59,000
You know what?

1635
01:44:59,100 --> 01:45:03,460
Maybe the shear needs to be a standard exploration thing to bring.

1636
01:45:05,620 --> 01:45:07,140
It's also useful in the nether.

1637
01:45:09,060 --> 01:45:10,860
It's also useful when you see sheep.

1638
01:45:11,620 --> 01:45:12,100
Right?

1639
01:45:18,100 --> 01:45:20,740
Kind of want to try and shear ODB.

1640
01:45:22,080 --> 01:45:23,920
